[N 28-29 Wetlands: Dun Modr and the Dragonmaw]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\One loop through the eastern Wetlands: Howin, the Dragonmaw camp and Retreat, the raptor nests, Dun Modr and the Thandol Span with a hop into Arathi, then the Menethil hand-ins and the boat to Auberdine.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 28-29|r  -  chapter 18 leaves you at Howin Kindfeather's camp on the Dun Algaz junction, about level 29, hearth = Sentinel Hill (it stays there: chapter 22 needs it). One counter-clockwise loop through the east Wetlands: Howin and the Dragonmaw camp, Dragonmaw Retreat and the raptor nests, back to the Greenwarden and Howin, then Dun Modr, the Thandol Span and Arathi, and Menethil. About 27,000 quest XP on the solo/duo road (the level 30 ding falls near its end) and 36,000 more in the |cFFFF0000GROUP|r blocks; every GROUP step is optional and skipping one costs nothing else.
[OC]|cffffcc00Log:|r you arrive with War Banners (464), From the Ashes (98221), This Land Was Their Land (98230), Crimson Crate Delivery (98240), Crocs of the Sky (98072), Fall of Dun Modr (472), In Search of The Excavation Team (306), Sida's bag (470) if you took it, and the carried ones (98209, 98815, shaman Call of Water 94500, Gleaning Our Future 98310 if you took it).
[OC]|cffffcc00Human hunters:|r the digest also flags Razormaw Needling (98245) and Trying Times (98246) as not offered to Humans on Wowhead; if Howin does not offer one, skip the line.

[OC]|cffffffffThe Greenwarden, Howin and the Angerfang camp|r  -  all within 12 units of the junction you stand on (Howin's camp): take every accept first, then work outward
[OC][A Shaman] Ghost Wolf for the road legs (junction - Dun Modr, Menethil - camp), off before every pull
[OC][A Hunter] Aspect of the Cheetah for the road legs (junction - Dun Modr, Menethil - camp), swap back before every pull
Walk 7 units east to the clearing. At [TAR1244 Rethiel the Greenwarden], [QA275 Blisters on The Land] (12 Fen Creepers, see the run back) [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r At [TAR1244 Rethiel the Greenwarden], [QA98283 Carnage] (the head comes from the raptor nests, below) [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1244 Rethiel the Greenwarden], [QA95646 Horrors in the Highland] (accept only: the root core drops from a Highland Horror inside the Excavation Site, chapter 22 closes it) [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
Walk back west to the road. At [TAR270637 Howin Kindfeather], [QT98230] [QT98240] [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
At [TAR270637 Howin Kindfeather], [QA98245 Razormaw Needling] [QA98246 Trying Times] [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
At [TAR270637 Howin Kindfeather], [QA98300 Word to Ironforge] (a missive for King Magni - chapter 24 hands it in) [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r At [TAR270637 Howin Kindfeather], [QA98291 Death to the Dragonmaw] [QA98297 Stopping the Cycle] [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Howin's quests:|r Razormaw Needling = 10 Razormaw Incisors from the raptors of the north-east nests (|cffffcc00drop rate not in the DB|r: a short farm). Trying Times = 12 Perfect Razormaw Eggs from nest objects the DB has no coordinates for: look for them among the same raptors. Death to the Dragonmaw = 8 Reclaimers, 5 Soulbinders and 3 Infiltrators in Dragonmaw Retreat. Stopping the Cycle = the Subdued Dragonspawn at the Dragonmaw Gates, far east

[OC]|cffffffffAngerfang Encampment|r  -  the largest Dragonmaw orc camp (45.7,45.4 on warcraft.wiki.gg), 5 units south-west of Howin: level 26-30, non-elite except the rare Battlemaster
Kill [TAR1034 Dragonmaw Raider] and the Swamprunners and Centurions for 8 Dragonmaw War Banners [QC464] [G45.6,45 Wetlands]
Bandage to 125: Heavy Wool Bandages from the Dragonmaw and Dark Iron wool until First Aid 125, which is what the Expert book in chapter 25 needs [G45.6,45 Wetlands]
[OC]War Banners is |cff66ff66normal|r (TUGs takes them in one pass through the camp; the drop rate is not in the DB). The Dragonmaw Battlemaster (30 rare elite, ~1,000 HP in the Classic DB) walks the middle at 45.3,44.4 and drops banners too: pull him with both of you or leave him
Click the four Attack Plans lying about the camp (Menethil Harbor, Thelsamar, Southshore, Ironforge) to burn them [QC98221] [G47.4,45.8 Wetlands]
[OC]The DB has no spawn for the plans, so no coordinates: they lie inside the camp around the catapults (47.4,47.0). Leave the catapults alone for now - Nek'rosh's Gambit needs War Banners handed in at Menethil first (the last block of the chapter)

[OC]|cffffffffDragonmaw Retreat and the raptor nests|r  -  east of the Greenwarden: dense level 23-31 country (the DB lists ~330 Reclaimer spawns alone), whelps and Dragonmaw on the near side, raptors in the north, the Dragonmaw Gates at the far east edge. West half of the Retreat first, the gates last, then swing north
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Click the Dragonmaw Armaments on the ground at the Retreat's western edge [QA98293 Forced Disarmament] [G58.9,45.1 Wetlands]
Kill [TAR1069 Crimson Whelp] and the Red, Lost and Flamesnorting Whelps (level 23-27, non-elite) for 8 Pristine Crimson Scales [QC98072] [G65.3,42.4 Wetlands]
[OC]Crocs of the Sky: |cffffcc00drop rate not in the DB|r, but four whelp types with ~70 spawn points around 60-70,33-52: a short pass, not a grind
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Kill 8 [TAR271351 Dragonmaw Reclaimer], 5 Dragonmaw Soulbinders and 3 Dragonmaw Infiltrators [QC98291] [G66.6,45.9 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Click every Dragonmaw Armaments you pass until you hold 30 [QC98293] [G68,45 Wetlands]
[OC]Forced Disarmament: the 30 pickups are objects the DB has no coordinates for, so there is no map to follow: sweep the Retreat once while you kill for Death to the Dragonmaw and count as you go
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Kill the [TAR271373 Subdued Dragonspawn] at the Dragonmaw Gates [QC98297] [G76.8,45.8 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Use the Goaz Stone beside [TAR271338 Ados], kill what wakes and loot the heart [QC98310,1] [G77,47.2 Wetlands]
[OC]The DB gives the Subdued Dragonspawn no level. The |cffffcc00Red Dragonspawn|r beside the gate (57 ELITE, ~79,48) is far out of your league: pull only what stands on your side and never walk through
[OC]Ados is the first of four hearts for Gleaning Our Future (98310, from Whelgar): Neru and Modr follow in the Dark Iron country, Golm stands by Hervdana's cave in the far south (chapter 22 hands the quest in at Whelgar). The DB gives these four no HP, only Modr and Golm a level (32): treat each as an elite
Kill [TAR1018 Highland Razormaw] and Elder Razormaws at the nests for 10 Razormaw Incisors [QC98245] [G66,31 Wetlands]
[OC]Razormaws are level 27-29, non-elite (~850-950 HP in the Classic DB): 59 spawn points, 45 of them around 65-74,25-39. The rare elite |cffffcc00Razormaw Matriarch|r (31, ~1,100 HP) sits at 69.9,29.2: leave her unless you are three
Gather 12 Perfect Razormaw Eggs from the nests as you pass them [QC98246] [G67.5,31 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Kill [TAR271336 Carnage] at 69.5,29.2 and loot Carnage's Head [QC98283] [G69.5,29.2 Wetlands]
[OC]Carnage: the DB gives him no level or elite flag (a new Forever boss, standing where it also puts the Razormaw Matriarch): treat him as an elite and bring the tank. The quest also wants Malignant Rotclaw Flesh from the level-25 Maddened Rotclaws that cover the highland between the Greenwarden and the nests (|cff66ff66normal|r: kill the ones in your way)
Walk back west along y 36-41 and kill 12 [TAR1040 Fen Creeper] [QC275] [G53.2,36.5 Wetlands]
[OC]Fen Creepers (24-25) are |cffffcc00sparse|r: the DB has only 19 spawn points for the whole north of the zone. Loop 53.2,36.5 - 55.0,37.2 - 54.0,41.4, then 47.6,32.8 and 46.4,29.2, and kill every one you see
